an an unauthorized commercial exploitation.\", \"summary\": \"The Rameshwari Photocopy Service owner argues that course packs contain only required readings and important sections, justifying the reproduction of copyrighted material as a necessary educational tool.\"}, \"3\": {\"original\": \"The law in India does not warrant judging course packs by whether they\", \"rephrased\": \"The Delhi High Court bench asserts that Indian law does not warrant judging the legality of course packs by whether they have become textbooks, but rather by considering whether the inclusion of copyrighted works is justified by the specific educational purpose of the course pack. This legal framework requires a purpose-based analysis to determine if the distribution of course packs constitutes fair use or copyright infringement.\", \"summary\": \"The Delhi High Court bench asserts that Indian law requires judging course pack legality based on whether the inclusion of copyrighted works is justified by the educational purpose, rather than by whether the packs have become textbooks.\"}}",
